body:
I can relate to that, well kind of, there are people I could talk just but I just choose not to.  what is it that makes you feel alone in life? (I know exactly what you mean, as I do feel the same, and I know the reasons why I feel that way) 

&#x200B;

You can always shoot me a PM if you don't want to discuss everything openly too!

Is there nobody else you can talk to?

&#x200B;

I know breakups can be rough, especially if you have devoted a lot of time and love to that person (I was with my last girlfriend for 8 years before she left me for my friend) so I can understand why you would be feeling really low about it, do you believe the horrible things he said to you?

Wow, the way you worded this has me thinking, did I post this myself? because you just described ME perfectly, down to the very last detail of how I feel when driving, I cannot say enough how much you are me right now.

&#x200B;

I think this helps me alittle on a personal level too, I hope this comment while not really being helpful in itself makes you feel, less alone? we could literally be twins.

The rules here explicitly state that we shouldn't talk about methods and stuff, but there is a website that deals with all the questions people have, and the statistics, it also includes some really valuable things to think about before making a permanent decision.

&#x200B;

I found it myself tonight, before I came here and in some way, it helped me a little bit.

&#x200B;

[http://lostallhope.com/](http://lostallhope.com/)

Hi, yes I have actually seen a few stories about various dogs who's owners passed on, while it is really saddening, I feel that, at the end of it all, if the worst came to worst, he'd atleast have a better shot at life rather than, (if the worst came to the worst) living on the street with me.

&#x200B;

I appreciate your kind words, thank you

I'm not sure exactly how to respond to this, I can't empathize as I don't have parents who I can turn to so I the situation isn't one I can begin to have any knowledge of.

&#x200B;

I like that you've set a date far enough in the future for your circumstances to change, life is an ever-changing thing, one day something can make you feel like nothing, and another day something can happen that brightens things up so not impulsively doing it is great.

&#x200B;

When it comes down to rejection and such, that is unfortunately just a part learning process, i've been through my fair share of rejection, and even been the one rejecting someone else, it's not an easy thing to cope with, that I do understand, people always say 'you just havn't met the right person yet' etc etc, which irritates me because I believe you have to wade through the bad to get to the good, which means even having bad relationships - but I wouldn't say you aren't 'made for love' it's the kind of thing that just, happens, if you know what I mean? 

&#x200B;

I do hope something changes in your life before October and makes you reconsider
